{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_45_863666533#4_1634967200","relevance":2,"reason":"The snippet gives a direct statistic from the Washington Post database about unarmed Black and white people fatally shot by police in 2019 and 2015, but the host document is a political forum thread with chatter rather than a dedicated, authoritative evidence page.","learned":"A commonly repeated Washington Post statistic is that police fatally shot nine unarmed Black people and 19 unarmed white people in 2019, down from 38 and 32 in 2015."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1449","reason":"Continue this Washington Post-focused query in case the next results include the original database or more authoritative articles using the same statistics."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1449"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_45_863666533#5_1634968587","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1449","rank":2,"snippet":"county 123urout Pastafarian The answer is 19 unarmed whites. Guess how many unarmed blacks were shot? king of the county Pastafarian MidnightMax MidnightMax Pastafarian Pastafarian MidnightMax Pastafarian MidnightMax king of the county king of the county king of the county king of the county Pastafarian Pastafarian Pastafarian Spike , Chester and Sylvester Pastafarian Join the conversation \" , \"segment\": \"? ? ? ? 9 The police <cover>fatally shot nine unarmed blacks and 19 unarmed whites in 2019, according to a Washington Post database, down from 38 and 32, respectively, in 2015. The Post defines “unarmed” broadly to include such cases as a suspect in Newark, N.J., who had a loaded handgun in his car during a police chase. In 2018 there were 7,407 black homicide victims. Assuming a comparable number of victims last year, </cover>those nine unarmed black victims of police shootings represent 0.1% of all African-Americans killed in 2019. By contrast, a police officer is 18½ times more likely to be killed by a black male than an unarmed black male is to be killed by a police officer. Quote Link to post Share on other sites king of the county Posted June 3, 2020 king "}}
