{"request":{"op":"document","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_57_591732046#0_839444811"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_57_591732046#0_839444811","document":"Fatal Force 2019 - Washington Post ... 999 999 Search the database 990 people were fatally shot by police in 2018 Where the 2019 shootings took place The Post's reporting on fatal police shootings The story must be told. Washington Post investigation: Murder with impunity More than 210,000 students have experienced gun violence at school since Columbine  ... Fatal Force 2019 - Washington Post 999 Search the database State Alabama 11 Alaska 7 Arizona 35 Arkansas 21 California 135 Colorado 36 Connecticut 4 D.C. 1 Delaware 2 Florida 64 Georgia 37 Hawaii 7 Idaho 7 Illinois 13 Indiana 16 Iowa 5 Kansas 9 Kentucky 15 Louisiana 20 Maine 3 Maryland 19 Massachusetts 5 Michigan 13 Minnesota 11 Mississippi 18 Missouri 28 Montana 6 Nebraska 6 Nevada 11 New Hampshire 2 New Jersey 12 New Mexico 18 New York 23 North Carolina 34 Ohio 24 Oklahoma 34 Oregon 18 Pennsylvania 14 South Carolina 18 South Dakota 3 Tennessee 33 Texas 108 Utah 12 Vermont 3 Virginia 10 Washington 36 West Virginia 13 Wisconsin 18 Wyoming 1 Gender Male 956 Female 43 Unknown 0 Race White 405 Black 249 Hispanic 163 Other 41 Unknown 141 Age Under 18 14 18 to 29 268 30 to 44 368 45 and up 282 Unknown 67 Mental illness Yes 215 No or unknown 784 Weapon Gun 599 Knife 172 Vehicle 64 Toy weapon 30 Other 60 Unarmed 54 Unknown 20 Body camera Yes 136 No or unknown 863 Fleeing the scene Car 173 Foot 138 Other 21 Not fleeing 593 Undetermined 74 999 people shot and killed by police Michael Vincent Davis, a 49-year-old White man armed with a gun, was shot on Dec. 31, 2019, in Cross Lanes, W.Va. West Virginia Male White 45 and up No/unknown mental illness Gun No body cam recording Fleeing by foot Sources: WOWK 13 News • apnews Terry Hudson, a 57-year-old Black man armed with a gun, was shot on Dec. 31, 2019, in an apartment in Omaha, Neb. Nebraska Male Black 45 and up No/unknown mental illness Gun Body cam recording Not fleeing Sources: KETV • ABC News 1 of 999 990 people were fatally shot by police in 2018 There were have been 9 more fatal shootings in 2019 than in 2018. Fatal police shootings by year 0 200 400 600 800 1,000 Jan. April July Oct. Dec. 2015 994 2016 961 2017 986 2018 990 2019 999 Where the 2019 shootings took place Each marks the location of a deadly shooting. Shootings per million people 0 9.5 HI AL AR AZ CA CO CT DE FL GA IA ID IL IN KS KY LA MA MD ME MI MN MO MS MT NC ND NE NH NJ NM NV NY OH OK OR PA RI SC SD TN TX UT VA VT WA WI WV WY AK There are 54 shootings with unverified locations that are not shown on the map. The Post's reporting on fatal police shootings Months after a fatal police shooting, a young officer turns his gun on himself Dec. 19, 2018 Fatal police shootings of unarmed people have significantly declined, experts say May 7, 2018 Nationwide, police shot and killed nearly 1,000 people in 2017 Jan. 6, 2018 In two years, police killed 86 people brandishing guns that look real — but aren’t Dec. 18, 2016 In fatal shootings by police, 1 in 5 officers’ names go undisclosed April 1, 2016 The story must be told. Your subscription supports journalism that matters. Try 1 month for $1 About this story The Washington Post's database contains records of every fatal shooting in the United States by a police officer in the line of duty since Jan. 1, 2015. In 2015, The Post began tracking more than a dozen details about each killing — including the race of the deceased, the circumstances of the shooting, whether the person was armed and whether the person was experiencing a mental-health crisis — by culling local news reports, law enforcement websites and social media, and by monitoring independent databases such as Killed by Police and Fatal Encounters.","ok":true,"op":"document"}}
