{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_908630318#4_1870901197","relevance":3,"reason":"This USA Today opinion article is dedicated to fatal police shootings of unarmed Black Americans and directly provides frequency evidence: police fatally shot about 1,000 civilians annually over the prior five years; Washington Post data showed 14 unarmed Black and 25 unarmed white victims in 2019; unarmed Black shooting victims were down 63% from 2015.","learned":"Washington Post Fatal Force data is cited for about 1,000 fatal police shootings annually, 14 unarmed Black and 25 unarmed white victims in 2019, and a 63% decline in unarmed Black fatal shooting victims from 2015."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1464","reason":"The current query is yielding directly relevant documents with annual police-killing and unarmed-victim counts, so continue to look for more grade-3 evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1464"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_765406444#1_1480350155","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1464","rank":3,"snippet":"765406444#1_1480350155\" , \"end_char\": 2454.000000 , \"headings\": \"These 4 charts describe police violence in America These 4 charts describe police violence in America Key Points Police killed 3 people per day last year Killings per capita vary across cities Police are almost never charged after killings Dozens of police killed <cover>annually \" , \"segment\": \"Jim Vondruska | NurPhoto | Getty Images Protests over the death of George Floyd entered their seventh day on Monday as cities across the country imposed curfews and deployed police in riot gear to control demonstrators. Floyd, a black man, was killed in police custody in Minneapolis one week ago. Video taken by bystanders showed a white police officer kneeling on Floyd’s neck as the unarmed </cover>man lay handcuffed and cried out that he could not breathe. The officer, Derek Chauvin, has been charged with murder. The criminal complaint, issued on Friday, accuses Chauvin of having his knee on Floyd’s neck for eight minutes and 46 seconds, including for nearly three minutes after Floyd was nonresponsive. VIDEO 2:06 02:06 Scenes from protests, riots across the U.S. "}}
