{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_365309099#6_649186739","relevance":3,"reason":"The article is dedicated to the problem of counting people killed by police and provides direct frequency evidence from multiple databases: Killed by Police counted 714 deaths that year through Monday, Fatal Encounters recorded more than 7,300 over about a decade and a half, and The Guardian counted 704 U.S. police killings that year, including 150 classified as unarmed.","learned":"Fatal Encounters, Killed by Police, and The Guardian's Counted all provide direct police-killing counts; The Guardian reported 704 killed that year including 150 unarmed, while Fatal Encounters had more than 7,300 over roughly 15 years."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1470","reason":"This Fatal Encounters/unarmed query is producing highly relevant database-based evidence on counts of people and unarmed victims killed by police, so continue for more grade-3 results."}}
