{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_365309099#5_649184839","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment of an article dedicated to how police-killing counts are tracked, giving direct evidence from multiple databases: Killed by Police counted 714 deaths so far that year, Fatal Encounters recorded more than 7,300 over about 15 years, and The Guardian counted 704 people killed by U.S. police that year including 150 unarmed.","learned":"Multiple independent databases converged on roughly 700 U.S. police killings partway through the year, with The Guardian classifying 150 as unarmed."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1470","reason":"Continue this productive Fatal Encounters/unarmed query to find more database-backed documents quantifying police killings and unarmed victims."}}
